  "subtitle": "A household knitting machine whose program is a deck of punched cards — Jacquard's idea, on a kitchen counter",
  "why_scout_cares": "A domestic flatbed knitting machine whose every pattern was punched by hand into a card and fed through a reader: one card row = one knitted row, each punched hole switching a needle into a different cam path so it knits, slips, or tucks. It is the Jacquard loom and the IBM punch card sitting on a kitchen counter — a physical, punched 'program' that runs to create fabric instead of compute. No knitting machine exists anywhere in the collection.",
